dividuals, children with chronic illnesses, and critically ill patients. It often arises from inadequate nutrient intake, malabsorption, or increased metabolic demands due to conditions such as cancer, severe burns, and chronic diseases like cystic fibrosis and EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease).\n\nIn hospitalized patients, \"\"DESNUTRICIÓN\"\" can complicate recovery and is often assessed through nutritional screening tools. It is prevalent among surgical patients, those with dysphagia, and individuals undergoing aggressive treatments, as inadequate nutrition can lead to weakened immune function, muscle wasting, and prolonged hospital stays. The condition can also affect the effectiveness of medications and is associated with various health issues, including complications like quilothorax and ascitic chylous.\n\n\"\"DESNUTRICIÓN\"\" is recognized as a significant public health issue affecting both developing and developed countries, necessitating dietary assessment and intervention to prevent and treat malnutrition. Nutritional support, including enteral or parenteral nutrition, may be required for patients unable to meet their caloric needs through oral intake alone. The healthcare system aims to identify, prevent, and treat this condition to improve patient outcomes and quality of life.\",74\r\n2336,CICLOSPORINA,\"Ciclosporina is an immunosuppressive medication that is primarily used in the treatment of complications following organ transplants. It has been tested for its efficacy in treating alcoholic liver disease (ALD) but has not shown significant clinical benefits. The drug can lead to various side effects, including diarrhea and neurological issues, which may improve upon discontinuation of the medication. Additionally, ciclosporina can contribute to the development of hypomagnesemia in patients undergoing chemotherapy and may cause alterations in lipid metabolism. It is important to note that the levels of ciclosporina in the body can be increased by the consumption of grapefruit juice, and the medication may also interact with weight loss drugs.\",6\r\n2335,CICLOFOSFAMIDA,\"Ciclofosfamida is a medication that serves multiple purposes in medical treatment. It is primarily recognized as an immunosuppressive drug, which is utilized in clinical trials to address inflammatory responses in brain lesions of patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). Additionally, ciclofosfamida is commonly used in oncological treatments. However, it is important for patients to take this medication with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. It is also noteworthy that ciclofosfamida can lead to malabsorption and malnutrition in patients, highlighting the need for careful monitoring during its use.\",2\r\n610,PÉRDIDA DE MASA MUSCULAR,\"PÉRDIDA DE MASA MUSCULAR, or loss of muscle mass, is a significant indicator of severe malnutrition and is assessed during the global subjective evaluation. This condition can arise from malnutrition and is frequently worsened by dysphagia, particularly in patients suffering from neurological diseases.\",2\r\n13312,ALTERACIONES CICATRIZACIÓN,Alteraciones cicatrización are complications in wound healing that can arise from poor nutritional status in cancer patients.,1\r\n3230,COSTES POR PROCESO,\"The costs associated with medical processes, which can increase due to malnutrition during hospitalization\",1\r\n1695,DESNUTRICIÓN LEVE,A classification of malnutrition characterized by a Body Mass Index (BMI) between 17 and 18.4.,1\r\n1697,DESNUTRICIÓN GRAVE,A classification of malnutrition characterized by a Body Mass Index (BMI) less than 16.,1\r\n4968,SÍNDROME DE WERNICKE-KORSAKOFF,\"Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome is a neurological disorder caused by thiamine deficiency, often associated with chronic alcoholism and malnutrition, leading to confusion and memory issues.\",1\r\n2516,ENFERMEDAD ONCOLÓGICA,\"The entity \"\"ENFERMEDAD ONCOLÓGICA\"\" refers to a type of cancer that can significantly impac